Built LangChain Myself
-----------------------

build these modules one by one:

my_langchain/
│
├── llm.py            # Connect to Groq/OpenAI/Gemini
├── prompts.py        # Prompt templates
├── memory.py         # Conversation history
├── chains.py         # Multi-step workflows
├── agents.py         # Agent orchestration
├── tools.py          # Weather, Search, Calculator
├── loaders.py        # PDF/CSV loaders
├── splitter.py       # Text chunking
├── embeddings.py     # Create embeddings
├── vectorstore.py    # FAISS/Chroma interface
├── retriever.py      # Retrieve relevant chunks
└── rag.py            # Combine retrieval + LLM

This is conceptually how LangChain evolved: it started with a small abstraction over LLM calls, 
then gradually added reusable components for common AI application tasks as developers encountered them.
Rather than inventing all of these ideas, Harrison Chase packaged them into a consistent, modular framework that developers could reuse across projects

